Travel Assistant with Parallel Tool Use
This project demonstrates an LLM-powered Travel Assistant built with LangChain that can search for hotels, calculate costs with taxes, and execute multiple tool calls in parallel within a multi-turn conversation.

🚀 Overview
Large Language Models (LLMs) excel at natural language understanding and generation, but they face inherent limitations when it comes to real-time knowledge, precise arithmetic, and external actions. This application bridges those gaps by equipping an LLM with custom Python tools:

Hotel Search (query_hotels): Closes the knowledge gap by querying a database for live hotel availability, pricing, and ratings.

Cost Calculator (calculate_total_cost): Closes the capability gap by performing precise arithmetic for nightly rates, durations, and taxes.

🛠️ Key Features
Tool Binding (.bind_tools): Dynamically attaches Python functions (along with their signatures, type hints, and docstrings) to the LLM so it knows when and how to invoke them.

Parallel Tool Execution: Automatically handles scenarios where the LLM requests multiple independent tool calls in a single turn (e.g., calculating totals for multiple hotels simultaneously).

Robust Message Flow: Manages a structured conversation history using SystemMessage, HumanMessage, AIMessage (with tool_calls), and ToolMessage results.

